    "solution": "Advance to the lip and watch the moth approach its far turn. Jump and dash across the descending vertical patrol to intercept the larger moth route on its return. Cut down without Jump for a low rebound; continue right to meet the second moth as it returns. Hold Jump with the second cut, then dash up-right from the loft through the space behind the upper patrol. The two moths are consumed, so missing either interception cannot be repaired by standing on a target.",
    "nearestExisting": "F33 preserves launch speed after a combat setup, while B54 introduces two fixed rebound heights. Here both targets are moving and disappear when cut: the first interception position determines the second, and the upper patrol punishes simply taking the highest rebound immediately.",
    "novelty": "Intercept a predictable moving launch target when its return creates the next safe angle",
