    "designNotes": "Both moth paths share a deterministic 180-frame clock, so the arrival is learnable rather than random enemy behaviour. They move at different horizontal speeds. The low first rebound meets the second target; a saved loft-first shortcut instead runs into the upper patrol. The exit\u2019s thorned western face prevents a low dash followed by a free climb.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The final loft and patrol crossing remain demanding. The receiving shelf is eight tiles wide; an alternate departure two frames later passes.",
